WEBVTT

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.450
<i>2125 AD,</i>

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.370
<i>Thirty years</i>

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.370
<i>since the discovery of a strange disease</i>
<i>which transforms humans into insects.</i>

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.790
<i>During that time,</i>

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.950
<i>humanity lost two-thirds</i>
<i>of its population.</i>

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.250
<i>The body hardens</i>
<i>within approximately ten minutes.</i>

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>It becomes resilient</i>
<i>to knives and even bullets.</i>

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:57.200
<i>As proposed by Emeth Chilio in his book</i>
Evolution to the Headless,

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.620
<i>it is a violent 20-minute transformation</i>
<i>from human to insect.</i>

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.250
<i>The evolution begins with the extremities</i>

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.330
<i>and progresses to the body,</i>
<i>neck, then head.</i>

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.330
<i>In order to eliminate</i>
<i>the threat they pose,</i>

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.580
<i>the head of the afflicted must be</i>
<i>removed within that 20 minutes.</i>

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.950
<i>Little Bo Peep</i>

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.410
<i>Has lost her sheep</i>

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:39.000
<i>And can't tell where to find them</i>

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.870
<i>Leave them alone</i>

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.950
<i>And they will come home</i>

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.750
<i>And bring their tails</i>

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.500
<i>Behind them</i>

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.750
<i>Little Bo Peep...</i>

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.290
An insect.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:48.700
It's still new.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:50.910
Jin.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.450
-You'd better be keeping watch, Kidow.
-Let's head back while we can.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.290
If I run away from treasure with my tail
between my legs,

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.700
I'll tarnish my reputation as a merchant!

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.200
Bugs eat people.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.410
Then old Jin snatches up
what's left behind!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.040
And your job as the Exterminator is
to escort me.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.410
This industrial system's well-built!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.580
Whoa, a whole water filter case!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:35.580
Look, Kidow! A generator!
It's even the newest model!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.080
This was well worth the trip.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.450
Just look at this pile of treasure.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.200
By God, if you damaged my treasure...!

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.410
Jin, we got bugs!

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.870
Kidow, you're up!

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.160
Huh, why?

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.290
Go after them!

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.410
Just great!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.450
Below!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:32.830
Ilie!

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.580
Kidow, where are you going?

00:05:58.870 --> 00:05:59.700
Ilie!

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:12.750
You okay, Kidow?

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.120
Kidow!

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.250
Don't! Kidow...

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.200
Please don't come back and haunt me.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.580
I promise to take good care
of your belongings.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.410
No way! They're still alive.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:23.790
Are you... an Exterminator?

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.160
Yeah.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.950
Please... look after my daughter...

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:32.910
Ilie.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.200
Please take her...

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.000
to her mother...

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.200
Tania.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.080
Please.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:50.870
Please.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:53.830
Okay.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.790
Your daughter is in safe hands.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.500
Rest easy.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.750
That was reckless with a kid...

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.000
Is she breathing?

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.080
I think so.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.870
Hey, she's awake, Kidow.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:39.910
Dad! Where's my dad?

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:41.370
Where's Dad?

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:44.290
Calm down, little girl.
We're right by the insect cage.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.700
-Let go of me! My dad's hurt!
-If we make a racket--

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.200
He needs to be treated!

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.120
It's too late.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:50.540
No! Dad!

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:52.790
Dad!

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:53.830
Dad!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.370
He's already dead. Come on.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.790
No, I can't just leave him there.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.080
Just let me go!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.500
Hey, I don't think she deserved that!

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.080
Your father's dying wish

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:13.750
was that you be entrusted to me.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.910
So, until we find your mother,
that's how it is.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:20.330
But I can't help someone
who won't help themselves.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.450
If you want to throw your life away,
go ahead.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.410
Kidow...

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.830
You should probably ice that.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:45.580
Thank you.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.700
Sorry, this guy's a little rough.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:03.200
What's the matter?

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:04.660
Does it hurt?

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:06.910
Look, she's hurt!

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.580
You happy now, you sadistic monster!

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.290
Shut up and drive!

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.000
Dad!

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:14.790
Dad!

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.040
Dad!

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.620
-Go on.
-Right, thanks.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.200
Still burning that midnight oil?

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.830
Risked our lives just for this!

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:39.120
An Exterminator?

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:40.500
So what.

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:41.910
Thanks!

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.160
He's carsick.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.370
Like, give me a break, right?

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.120
Screw those Exterminators!

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.120
We don't need any of you.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.120
The Eastern Allied Forces'
E-05 Anti-Insect Tank Force

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.040
can protect the peace and order
of 05 just fine!

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:16.700
Got that?

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.160
The hell you say?

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.160
Bring it on!

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.160
Now, now.

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.910
Can't we all just hate the bugs
and have a drink?

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.750
Tanks, you say?

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.370
Screw Exterminators
and screw vigilante forces alike!

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.700
Somebody fill my glass!

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:47.750
Help me!

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.790
Three, four of them?

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:10.870
Damn it.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.910
-Look at all these damn Cagasters.
-Don't. You'll hit pedestrians.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:16.410
-Kidow!
-Sir!

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.120
Kidow! Where's your shotgun?

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.950
Get the hell out of the way, Exterminator!

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.200
Thanks, sir!

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:49.120
We'll circulate the document, so come
pick up the Extermination fee tomorrow.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:57.830
Thanks!

00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:58.830
Come again!

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:02.540
Water!

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:10.250
My, what a cute little guest.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.250
She's scared of you.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:18.040
Well, you're an ass.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.750
Hello, beautiful. What's your name?

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:23.750
Ilie.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.290
Hi, Ilie.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:26.700
We can talk later.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:29.160
Let her rest in my room for now.

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:30.700
Of course.

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:37.660
Don't worry. It's safe here.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:40.790
Come along, then.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:46.540
I'll be downstairs.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.580
Just call if you need something.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.120
I'll come right up.

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:17.830
She was trembling.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:26.000
She got attacked by bugs
and lost her father.

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:30.120
Then she gets here and meets
a freshly-afflicted Cagaster.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:32.540
She seems okay?

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.750
It might take a while.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.290
I see.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.910
Mario, can you find a woman named Tania?

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.540
<i>Her mother, I'm guessing.</i>

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.370
<i>Any other leads?</i>

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:46.950
<i>No.</i>

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.750
<i>Okay, I'll do what I can.</i>

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:56.620
What am I doing?

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:37.370
Exterminators are swords!

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:39.000
A killing instrument

00:16:39.500 --> 00:16:40.580
doesn't need a heart!

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.080
Cagasters aren't human.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.580
Decapitate them without hesitation!

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:53.080
No matter who they are.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.410
If you're an Exterminator,

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:57.250
you make a pile of corpses.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.540
You're a heartless instrument.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.660
What, she disappeared?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.200
It seems like she left
while I was busy doing prep work.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.950
You have to find her and bring her back.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.200
Where are you going, Kidow?

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:54.290
She left of her own accord.

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.660
Which means it's not our problem.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:58.750
You don't care what happens to her?

00:17:58.830 --> 00:17:59.750
No.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:02.000
I'm no longer obligated to look after her.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.200
What did you say?

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.790
Such a big city.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:11.290
No farms, no fields.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.200
It's so different from my village.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.950
There are so many people here,

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:20.000
but I don't know anybody.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:22.200
Dad...

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.500
I'm right here.

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:29.830
Dad!

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:32.080
Dad!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:43.160
Dad!

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:44.910
Dad!

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.080
No.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.370
I want to go home.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:58.500
Now departing for the Bazaar
via the eastern route.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:03.330
The east loop bus will be leaving
in five minutes via the South Gate.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.290
Wait! I'm getting on!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.500
I want to go to A-47!

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.660
I want to go home to A-47!

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.910
Does this bus go to A-47?

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:22.250
If a bus like this left the city,
we'd be dead in seconds.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.370
Now departing for the marketplace.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:28.790
Wait! Please take me to A-47!

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.370
Please stop!

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:32.120
Stop!

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:36.620
So, what's this ruckus all about?

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:40.370
Help, Jin!

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:43.370
They started fighting
after a little girl ran away.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.580
What?
I came all this way to return her photo.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.250
Why should I have to go look for
that brat?

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.330
Once you help her,

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:57.540
it's your responsibility
to see it through!

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.120
She just lost her father.

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:05.330
Stop measuring everything
by your own standards.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:14.040
Kidow...

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.450
It's no use.

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:20.870
He's not compassionate enough
to go out looking for a girl.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:22.660
You're wrong.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:25.700
<i>I'm sure he sees himself in her.</i>

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:27.790
<i>That idiot.</i>

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:40.250
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:43.160
Dumb-ass.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.200
This doesn't make sense.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.750
No, Dad!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.000
Dad!

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:55.660
Run away all you like.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:58.330
The fact is you're still alone.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:05.080
<i>I remember this feeling.</i>

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:36.000
No!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.120
No!

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:40.200
Cut it out!

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:42.910
Stay away!

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.700
Stop!

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:53.250
Don't go any further!

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:59.160
Jeez, do you want to die?

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:17.120
You little... You'd better apologize!

00:22:17.950 --> 00:22:19.660
Let's get out of here!

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:27.410
They didn't mean any harm.

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:30.370
You get a lot of bad people
around these parts.

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:34.750
That's why we sometimes put these on.

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:37.450
I'm Naji. What's your name?

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:41.910
I'm Ilie. Thank you
for helping me back there, Naji.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:47.500
Well, can't have that, can we?

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:48.830
Come with me!

00:22:59.160 --> 00:23:00.080
Thank you.

00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:03.660
Have you always lived here?

00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:06.200
You think this place is a dump, don't you?

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:07.620
Not at all!

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:12.250
This West Gate used to be the place to be.

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:16.120
<i>But one of the adults</i> <i>turned</i>
<i>into a Cagaster.</i>

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:19.910
<i>Everyone died because they couldn't</i>
<i>exterminate it in time.</i>

00:23:21.910 --> 00:23:25.790
They ended up blocking off the gate
to limit the losses.

00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:29.790
The residents trapped inside were burned
along with the bug. And here we are.

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:31.660
That's awful.

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:33.330
Who would do that?

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:35.250
Exterminators and the military.

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:38.660
Exterminators?

00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:49.370
Hey.

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:50.540
You seen this girl?

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:55.750
Grandpa, I'm back.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:57.250
This is my friend Ilie.

00:23:58.290 --> 00:23:59.330
Nice to meet you.

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:05.660
Oh... You picked up a girl?

00:24:07.080 --> 00:24:09.830
No! Just get dementia already,
you pervert!

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:11.700
Ilie, I'll show you something good!

00:24:22.040 --> 00:24:23.120
Pretty, isn't it?

00:24:23.660 --> 00:24:28.540
The West Gate sunset used to be
the main attraction in 05.

00:24:33.790 --> 00:24:37.250
Where did you come from?
You don't look familiar.

00:24:37.830 --> 00:24:39.950
-The Bazaar?
-No

00:24:42.160 --> 00:24:46.250
My home is in Area A, far west of here.

00:24:47.950 --> 00:24:48.870
These are good.

00:24:49.160 --> 00:24:50.080
Thanks.

00:24:55.580 --> 00:24:58.870
We hardly had any stores or even houses.

00:24:59.450 --> 00:25:01.580
There were more sheep than people.

00:25:03.250 --> 00:25:06.950
<i>I lived with my father, tending the sheep.</i>

00:25:08.250 --> 00:25:11.080
<i>Only the village mayor had electricity</i>
<i>and a telephone.</i>

00:25:11.950 --> 00:25:14.910
<i>We had to walk to a faraway well</i>
<i>to draw water.</i>

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:17.450
<i>When wild dogs showed up,</i>

00:25:17.870 --> 00:25:20.910
<i>we both stayed up until we drove them off.</i>

00:25:23.790 --> 00:25:25.950
But I can't go home anymore.

00:25:27.330 --> 00:25:29.080
And my dad's already...

00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:33.620
You know,

00:25:34.040 --> 00:25:35.700
I don't remember much

00:25:36.540 --> 00:25:39.620
about this place
before it was all burned down.

00:25:41.080 --> 00:25:42.620
When I become a grownup,

00:25:43.200 --> 00:25:45.120
this will be the home that I remember.

00:25:45.790 --> 00:25:48.290
When I told my grandpa
how frustrated I was

00:25:48.450 --> 00:25:52.160
that I couldn't remember
what it was like before,

00:25:52.910 --> 00:25:54.870
he told me, "Look at this sunset.

00:25:55.540 --> 00:26:01.160
Your hometown was and is the spot in 05
with the most beautiful sunset.

00:26:02.450 --> 00:26:04.830
Even if the Cagasters kill tons of people

00:26:05.410 --> 00:26:07.620
or the military burns down the cities,

00:26:08.450 --> 00:26:11.910
they can't destroy this sunset."

00:26:13.250 --> 00:26:16.500
So, this view is your hometown.

00:26:17.160 --> 00:26:19.250
This sunset will never change.

00:26:19.700 --> 00:26:21.450
This view is my home.

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:25.080
Even if the time comes
when I'll have to leave this place,

00:26:25.910 --> 00:26:28.120
I'll always be able to remember
this sunset.

00:26:28.950 --> 00:26:31.580
I won't be sad or frustrated.

00:26:32.330 --> 00:26:35.620
I can proudly remember that it was pretty.

00:26:36.750 --> 00:26:38.250
You can remember, too, Ilie.

00:26:40.120 --> 00:26:40.950
Yeah.

00:26:41.040 --> 00:26:46.620
<i>Little Bo Peep has lost her sheep</i>

00:26:47.200 --> 00:26:53.620
<i>And can't tell where to find them</i>

00:27:00.660 --> 00:27:04.540
<i>There was a tree in the forest</i>
<i>that bloomed white flowers.</i>

00:27:05.870 --> 00:27:08.450
<i>You could only see them briefly</i>
<i>in the spring,</i>

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:11.910
<i>but my dad said he was too busy to go.</i>

00:27:12.500 --> 00:27:16.450
<i>So, I broke the rules and snuck out</i>
<i>to see them by myself.</i>

00:27:23.620 --> 00:27:26.370
I'm sorry!
I was looking for the flower tree!

00:27:26.540 --> 00:27:27.910
But I couldn't find it.

00:27:29.870 --> 00:27:31.910
Ilie, look up.

00:27:38.790 --> 00:27:40.160
I won't forget either.

00:27:48.410 --> 00:27:50.160
I need to go back.

00:27:51.160 --> 00:27:53.200
There's someone who rescued me.

00:27:53.830 --> 00:27:56.870
But he's so mean.
He would just suddenly hit me.

00:27:56.950 --> 00:27:59.500
Seriously? Is it a guy?

00:27:59.660 --> 00:28:02.910
What man hits a girl? He's a sadist!
A pervert!

00:28:03.660 --> 00:28:06.080
But if he hadn't,

00:28:06.750 --> 00:28:11.290
<i>I think I would've sat down and cried,</i>
<i>waiting to die.</i>

00:28:12.330 --> 00:28:13.620
So, I have to go back.

00:28:14.370 --> 00:28:17.160
He might be upset with me now,

00:28:17.950 --> 00:28:20.660
but he might also be worried.

00:28:22.200 --> 00:28:24.950
I may not be able to go home
with my dad anymore,

00:28:25.870 --> 00:28:27.580
but I won't forget any of it.

00:28:28.410 --> 00:28:30.250
I won't run anymore.

00:28:30.910 --> 00:28:31.830
Yeah!

00:28:36.160 --> 00:28:39.000
But I ran away on my own.

00:28:39.910 --> 00:28:41.040
I even left a note.

00:28:41.450 --> 00:28:42.620
Oh, boy.

00:28:42.950 --> 00:28:43.870
Naji!

00:28:44.620 --> 00:28:46.700
What? Food won't be until later.

00:28:47.200 --> 00:28:51.540
No, a generous young man just stopped by.

00:28:52.580 --> 00:28:53.750
What is this?

00:28:54.080 --> 00:28:56.040
He didn't ask you some shady favor,
did he?

00:28:56.120 --> 00:28:59.290
No, rather just that I give this to her.

00:29:00.120 --> 00:29:02.450
Here, this is important to you, isn't it?

00:29:02.870 --> 00:29:05.700
-Yes.
-It was a handsome but sullen fellow.

00:29:05.950 --> 00:29:08.450
-Mr. Kidow.
-That's too bad.

00:29:08.950 --> 00:29:10.750
Looks like she already has a boyfriend.

00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:12.160
It's not like that!

00:29:13.160 --> 00:29:14.700
Ilie! See you later!

00:29:15.370 --> 00:29:16.540
Thanks for everything!

00:29:17.660 --> 00:29:21.870
Cute girls, generous guys.

00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:23.910
Today was a good day.

00:29:27.330 --> 00:29:30.200
He came to look for me, and I just...

00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:33.700
I was scared of Mr. Kidow, Ms. Mario,
and the whole city

00:29:34.330 --> 00:29:35.950
and just ran away from the diner.

00:29:36.500 --> 00:29:38.250
I'm not a little kid anymore.

00:29:40.290 --> 00:29:41.120
Wait!

00:29:42.160 --> 00:29:45.620
I'm sorry. You made a promise to my father

00:29:45.790 --> 00:29:51.040
and said you'd help me find my mother.
I'm sorry for selfishly running away!

00:29:53.580 --> 00:29:56.290
I don't break my promises with the dead.

00:29:56.700 --> 00:29:57.620
That's all.

00:29:58.370 --> 00:29:59.370
Mr. Kidow...

00:30:03.950 --> 00:30:05.910
Drop the mister. Kidow's fine.

00:30:06.540 --> 00:30:08.290
-Let's go, shorty.
-"Shorty"?

00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:09.910
Okay!

00:30:15.410 --> 00:30:16.790
-What's this?
-Don't touch it.

00:30:17.540 --> 00:30:19.790
-What is it?
-I told you not to touch it.

00:30:21.540 --> 00:30:24.540
Is this a battlefield?

00:30:24.910 --> 00:30:28.950
Just shut up and work. We need this
spotless before Ilie gets back.

00:30:29.080 --> 00:30:30.080
Right...

00:30:33.370 --> 00:30:34.540
Ilie!

00:30:36.290 --> 00:30:37.200
Ms. Mario.

00:30:37.660 --> 00:30:39.410
I'm so glad you're back.

00:30:39.750 --> 00:30:41.200
Ilie!

00:30:42.910 --> 00:30:45.120
-Welcome back, Ilie!
-Stay back! Jeez, so filthy!

00:30:45.200 --> 00:30:48.540
This guy's a handful
when you're not around, Ilie!

00:32:38.790 --> 00:32:41.370
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
